    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/model_routing.py `approve_supervisor_diff` stores `owner_approval.diverged_paths` and `approved_at`. It stores no content hash of the approved state. `record_retained_execution` copies the approval without comparing the current divergence to the approved paths. A digest check at finalization would prevent this.",
      "id": "approval-not-bound-to-content",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The owner approval is recorded as a list of diverged paths. It is not bound to a content digest. After approval the plan is `supervisor-retained`, so the early gate no longer checks divergence. Any supervisor edits made after the owner approved are silently covered by the approval."
    }
